WEBVTT

00:00:00.079 --> 00:00:01.730
Welcome to Resgrid Academy.

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:05.699
In this lesson, we will take an incident from intake to closeout.

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:10.789
Inconsistent call classification and unclear recipients create avoidable

00:00:10.789 --> 00:00:13.319
re-entry and uncertainty during dispatch.

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:16.809
We will explain the features, the setup decisions, and a

00:00:16.809 --> 00:00:18.700
practical way to check the result.

00:00:19.439 --> 00:00:23.100
A department adds Structure Fire and Medical call types, sets

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:27.680
Responding and On Scene statuses and connects its county CAD email feed.

00:00:28.139 --> 00:00:32.500
Consistent call types and statuses make dispatching, response tracking and

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:34.899
reporting reliable from the first call.

00:00:35.399 --> 00:00:38.889
The examples in this series use a fictional department and are teaching

00:00:38.889 --> 00:00:41.170
scenarios, not default settings.

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:43.480
Call types and priorities.

00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:47.109
The call types and priorities used to classify calls.

00:00:47.549 --> 00:00:50.990
Add the call types your dispatchers use and set their priorities.

00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:53.479
Personnel and unit statuses.

00:00:53.899 --> 00:00:58.700
The statuses members and units report, such as Responding or On Scene.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:02.949
Review the built-in statuses and add your own where your terms differ.

00:01:03.589 --> 00:01:04.729
Dispatch Settings.

00:01:05.219 --> 00:01:09.710
How calls page personnel: by group or by shift, and related

00:01:09.739 --> 00:01:11.270
automatic status changes.

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:15.169
Choose whether dispatch follows groups or shifts, and review

00:01:15.169 --> 00:01:16.940
the automatic status options.

00:01:17.569 --> 00:01:19.470
Email and CAD call intake.

00:01:19.839 --> 00:01:24.109
Create calls automatically from CAD, paging or email dispatches.

00:01:24.459 --> 00:01:27.469
Choose your CAD or paging format and connect the mailbox

00:01:27.469 --> 00:01:28.969
that receives dispatches.

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:31.489
Run cards and recommendations.

00:01:31.949 --> 00:01:35.000
Recommended resources for each call type or area.

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:39.899
Build run cards for your most common calls, then turn on recommendations.

00:01:40.539 --> 00:01:41.139
Calls.

00:01:41.549 --> 00:01:43.809
Active calls and their dispatch status.

00:01:44.269 --> 00:01:48.100
Collect your call types, the statuses members report while responding,

00:01:48.439 --> 00:01:52.850
and the details of any CAD or paging system that should create calls.

00:01:53.469 --> 00:01:54.120
New Call.

00:01:54.449 --> 00:01:56.009
Create and dispatch a call.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:00.159
Collect your call types, the statuses members report while responding,

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:04.389
and the details of any CAD or paging system that should create calls.

00:02:05.039 --> 00:02:06.159
Archived Calls.

00:02:06.590 --> 00:02:08.150
Closed and past calls.

00:02:08.579 --> 00:02:12.419
Collect your call types, the statuses members report while responding,

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:16.619
and the details of any CAD or paging system that should create calls.

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:18.210
Call templates.

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:22.569
Reusable call text and note templates that speed up call entry.

00:02:23.069 --> 00:02:26.900
Collect your call types, the statuses members report while responding,

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:31.049
and the details of any CAD or paging system that should create calls.

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:32.760
Check-in timers.

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:36.610
Timers that remind responders on a call to check in, with

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:38.249
escalation when they do not.

00:02:38.789 --> 00:02:42.630
Collect your call types, the statuses members report while responding,

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:47.279
and the details of any CAD or paging system that should create calls.

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:49.889
Text call intake and commands.

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:53.619
Create calls and accept member commands by text message.

00:02:53.959 --> 00:02:57.749
Collect your call types, the statuses members report while responding,

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:02.020
and the details of any CAD or paging system that should create calls.

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:03.529
Call Settings.

00:03:03.979 --> 00:03:08.050
The mailbox and format used to import calls from CAD or paging email.

00:03:08.459 --> 00:03:12.399
Collect your call types, the statuses members report while responding,

00:03:12.689 --> 00:03:16.580
and the details of any CAD or paging system that should create calls.

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:20.029
For the training scenario, work in this order.

00:03:20.489 --> 00:03:21.029
Step 1.

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:25.109
Configure call types, priorities, and response statuses.

00:03:25.539 --> 00:03:26.249
Step 2.

00:03:26.619 --> 00:03:30.950
Create a training call, confirm its map location, and choose recipients.

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:32.089
Step 3.

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:35.559
Review response progress, close the training call, and

00:03:35.559 --> 00:03:37.259
find it in archived calls.

00:03:37.899 --> 00:03:39.429
Now verify the result.

00:03:39.969 --> 00:03:43.100
Check the saved call details and intended recipients.

00:03:43.469 --> 00:03:46.630
Use a controlled communication test to evaluate delivery

00:03:46.630 --> 00:03:48.760
separately from the saved dispatch.

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:53.750
A common problem to watch for: Run-card recommendations require review.

00:03:54.189 --> 00:03:58.570
Shift routing, unit crew routing, group routing, and automatic status

00:03:58.570 --> 00:04:00.529
changes can affect different people.

00:04:01.179 --> 00:04:02.740
Your practice task is simple.

00:04:03.189 --> 00:04:05.569
Create a Medical training call for Station 1.

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:09.599
Confirm the location, recipients, status transitions,

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:11.699
closeout, and archived record.

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:15.960
Record the result, who owns the follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

